WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.058
An agent produces a spreadsheet.

00:00:08.138 --> 00:00:09.995
Every total in it is correct.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.198
The verifier opens the file with a reader
that returns cached values only,

00:00:18.278 --> 00:00:20.373
and openpyxl does not write them.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.026
The formula is stored as text.

00:00:26.106 --> 00:00:28.300
The result beside it was never computed,

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.086
and the container has no
spreadsheet application.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.228
On this benchmark a single failed
assertion loses the entire task.

00:00:39.308 --> 00:00:41.608
Six of the 87 are exposed to it.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.401
The correction has to be executable.

00:00:45.481 --> 00:00:48.580
The pack ships a script that calls
a spreadsheet engine

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.660
and writes the computed values back.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.615
Measurement was paired, one arm with
the library and one without.

00:00:59.695 --> 00:01:02.325
Three tasks converted and none regressed.

00:01:02.405 --> 00:01:05.100
The held out set was registered in advance

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.422
and returned a null.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.389
Seven packs, scoped to the Office formats
where the mechanism applies.

00:01:13.469 --> 00:01:16.575
Outside that set the library stays inactive.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.251
Both archives are attached.

00:01:20.331 --> 00:01:25.460
The practice worth carrying forward
is to read the verifier first.

